            <ArticleTitle>Efficacy of acupuncture for acute migraine attack: a multicenter single blinded, randomized controlled trial.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>623-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1526-4637.2012.01376.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">We aim to investigate the efficacy of acupuncture for acute migraine attacks comparing with sham acupuncture.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="DESIGN" NlmCategory="METHODS">The study was designed as a multicenter, single-blinded, randomized controlled clinical trial.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="SETTING AND PATIENTS" NlmCategory="METHODS">From March 2007 to February 2009, 150 patients were randomly allocated to verum or sham acupuncture group in a ratio of 1:1.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="INTERVENTIONS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Every patient received a verum or sham acupuncture treatment when having a migraine attack and, medications were allowed if the pain failed to be relieved two hours after the acupuncture.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="OUTCOME MEASURES" NlmCategory="METHODS">The primary outcome was visual analog scale (VAS) scores for pain, ranging from 0 (no pain) to 10 (worst pain ever).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The mean VAS scores 24 hours after treatment decreased from 5.7 ± 1.4 to 3.3 ± 2.5 in the verum acupuncture group, and from 5.4 ± 1.3 to 4.7 ± 2.4 in the sham acupuncture group. Significant differences existed between the two groups (P = 0.001).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">This trial suggested that verum acupuncture group was superior to sham acupuncture group on relieving pain and reducing the usage of acute medication.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Wiley Periodicals, Inc.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
